bc('WB25',[274,275,276],'Relative/absolute Advance and inherited code boundaries','Advance Down adds1.94in to preceding baseline; adding date+returns moves relative destination to3.61in. Absolute Line2 15/16returns2.94in even when preceding text already reaches3.33in. Caret before/after code gives different status; preview is separate. Up/Left/Right/Position are visible unselected leads, not extra executed steps.','L1 I3 P3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB25',[277,278,279],'Reference/target names, generation and repeated references','Both inserts named REF/TARGET at current reference and searched heading. Initial reference expects page2. Hard Page pushes target to3; explicit Generate5/Yes updates value. Multiple references may target same heading; graphs/tables/notes and other reference types remain leads. Cross-reference is native data requiring later codec and qualified runtime evidence.','D5 L3 I3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB25',[279,280,281],'Decimal alignment and separator locale','Tab+Tab Align precedes each row at same tab stop. First list uses period decimal/comma thousands; new configuration uses comma/period and second list retains that literal punctuation. Setting also affects Math/Tables; optional space alignment permits text alignment. Notice1639already matches1989step4; notice1851pointer has declared-page drift.','L1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB25',[281,282],'Normal versus extended/nested search and cancellation','Normal fortune search returns Not found; Extended enters endnote and finds same word. F2alone opens normal search, F1cancels prompt; Home/F2must be used for each further extended occurrence. After no more matches exit nested editor. Nested captions/headers/footnotes/endnotes/boxes and backward direction are source leads. Original menu-after5/7 differs from1852correction.','I3 L9 L10 G1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB25',[282,283,284,285],'Hyphenation resources, manual prompt and persistent setting','Source requires language dictionary WP{WP}US.LEX and associated .HYC; cached public prose only, resource files not opened. Yes/No inserts persistent hyphenation owners. Home/Down reformats current page. Page2may show Position hyphen prompt requiring manual intervention; later1853adds F1orEscape before reformat. Literal notice prints Home,@, not a reliable down-arrow encoding. Zone/full justification and missing resources remain variants needing runtime evidence.','T1 L1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB25',[283,284],'Soft hyphens and retained existing text','Reveal shows generated soft hyphens when unused; editing/print displays only line-end ones. Turning off does not erase existing soft hyphens: guided Delete removes personality hyphen. Ctrl+hyphen is optional manual insertion. No-hyphenation setting and already inserted owners have separate lifetimes; no automatic deletion inferred.','E1 T1 L1 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB25',[285,286],'INPUT message contexts and position','Three INPUT owners follow To/From/Subject with prompt strings; To and From use same name(s) message, Subject differs. Message belongs to native merge code and may include semicolon/space punctuation. Caption explanations and diagram hashes retained; no private MEMO content opened.','Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB25',[287,288],'Keyboard-input merge pause/resume and quit','MEMO.25primary with empty secondary pauses at INPUT. Enter alone adds line; Tab names multiple recipients; F9continues. Own sender/subject/body are open-ended exercises. While paused normal editing/format/Reveal may be used. Explicit stop route Merge Codes/ Quit1 exists while paused or running; exact cancellation artifact and refusal are unobserved.','I1 I3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB25',[289,290],'Phone list FIELD1/FIELD4 and repeated body formatting','Primary includes Tab Set3,FIELD1,Tab,FIELD4,return,PAGEOFF. Original CUSTOMER.WKB is selected, not WB24learner CUSTOMER. PAGEOFF suppresses inter-record hard page. Body Tab Set repeats for each merged record; this is an intentional comparison, not redundant instructions.','L1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB25',[291,292],'Initial Codes inherited once versus repeated body owners','Remove body Tab Set and define2.75in in Document Initial Codes. Reveal body does not expose initial-code content. Format applies once to merged result; first phone position3.75in includes1in margin. Notice1687declares274but candidate step4isprinted282; left-arrow removal applicability unresolved.','L1 I3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB25',[292,293],'Merge to printer ordered owners, memory and temp disk','Original numbered order PRINT then PAGEOFF is preserved. Later2026notice requires PAGEOFF beforePRINT and changes screenshot/prose. Source says PRINTsends letter and clears memory, reducing memory/disk temp needs for large merge; disk/file/printer failures are not exercised. No automatic printer replay or print artifact is produced.','P1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB25',[293],'Optional printer selection, learner LETTER.25 and unavailable Workbook Printer','Optional test requires choosing own printer before saving LETTER.25 (OCRLETTER25, visual includes dot) and merging CUSTOMER.WKB. Stored primary printer is used; default Workbook Printer is explicitly unsuitable for physical devices. Source conditional branch is retained, with no actual file/save/merge/print.','P1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
bc('WB25',[294,295,296,297],'Parallel columns with block protection and explicit column boundaries','Type3Parallel with Block Protect selected; columns On surrounds two-shot script. Hard Page ends each parallel column, while blank lines/italic transition headings outside code owner position text. Source directs caret Left twice before owners then Home/Home/Down after them. Source camera/narration creative text is bounded by hashes and locators rather than reproduced as new fixture.','L1 I3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB25',[297],'Optional script continuation and preview','Single final numbered instruction permits own camera-shot/story continuation or Print/View then Exit/No/No. Open-ended continuation has no finite invented target count. Guided two shots remain original160step total; optional prose not expanded into runtime IDs.','L1 P3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB25',[297,298],'Reveal split temporary versus persistent setup','Default editing11/Reveal10line partition can be resized with arrow movement or direct number. Guided Down6 then Enter gives larger editing window; Window11 restores. SetupShiftF1,2,6,6 changes persistent split; ordinary Window affects current session. Optional arbitrary edits are not enumerated.','I1 I3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB26',[302,303,304],'Compose aliases, character-set identities and later numbering','Compose accepts two keyboard characters for some glyphs, but most use set,index. Small filled bullet=*.,medium=**,small set4,3,half=/2,AE,e+apostrophe,sigma8,36,copyright4,23. Existing bullet identity inspected in Reveal then duplicate removed. Notice1354restructures opening steps1/2, not a renumbering of pinned1989original.','E2 I2 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB26',[303,304,305],'Native identity versus screen display and OCR','Source says over1700WordPerfect characters but screen font256/512. Copyright may display reverse-video rectangle without losing identity. OCRlQ/12 in half-character instructions corresponds to visual1/2glyph and /2input. Editing glyph availability, native encoding and printer output must be assessed separately. No claim all1700were exercised.','E2 I2 P3 Q1 Q2')
bc('WB26',[305,306,307],'Printer character availability and graphic fallback','CHARACTR.WKB is public-described teaching resource; its file is not opened. Initial Graphics QualityDoNotPrint shows only available printer characters. Medium enables graphic fallback for missing maps4/5/6; source preview checks depend on selected printer and graphics ability. High text quality overrides graphic resolution; Medium/Draft uses graphics setting. CancelF1returns Print, then Exit. No physical printing.','E2 I2 P1 P3 Q1 Q2')
